  "value": "text is file content: lines end with \"\\n\", except that a final line without a newline is still a line. Return the text of the last n lines exactly as they appear (keeping their newlines, and no newline after a final unterminated line), like tail -n n. If text has at most n lines return all of it; n = 0 returns \"\".",
